        rdfs:comment                   "Skirt panel of brocaded silk, Spitalfields, London 1743-1744"@en , "Skirt panel of brocaded silk consisting of several pieces. It is brocaded with coloured silks on an off white ground with a flush pattern. The design consists of bunches of flowers linked by string and tied in loose bows. The string is purple and yellow and the flowers are pale yellow, purple, tan and pink with leaves in two shades of green. \n\nIt has a tabby ground, the brocaded wefts are unbound and the flush pattern is formed by an interruption of the ground weave."@en ;
